course: dictionary
lesson: 2355
title: The cube
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cube is a solid shape with 6 square faces, and all the faces are the same size. A dice and a sugar cube are both cubes. «One cube has 6 + 12 + 8 = 26 faces, edges and corners together» tells you how many of each part a cube has: 6 faces, 12 edges and 8 corners.
explain: Cube can also mean a small block of something. «That is why an ice cube melts in your warm hand» is not about counting faces. Here the cube is a small block of ice. When a word has more than one meaning, the rest of the sentence tells you which one is meant.
explain: Cube can also be a verb. To cube a number means to multiply it by itself three times. «The cube of 2 is 8» because 2 × 2 × 2 = 8. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A cube has 6 faces, 12 edges and 8 corners.
fact: All the faces of a cube are squares of the same size.
fact: The volume of a cube is edge × edge × edge.
fact: Cube numbers start 1, 8, 27, 64, because 1 × 1 × 1 = 1, 2 × 2 × 2 = 8, 3 × 3 × 3 = 27 and 4 × 4 × 4 = 64.
fact: «Wombats are the only animals known to make cube-shaped droppings, which do not roll away.»
exercise: How many faces does a cube have? | 4 | 8 | 12 | *6
exercise: «The cube of 2 is 8.» What is the cube of 3? | 64 | 6 | 9 | *27
exercise: «That is why an ice cube melts in your warm hand.» In this sentence, what is an ice cube? | *A small block of ice | A cube shape with 12 edges | A number multiplied by itself | A grain of sugar
test: «One cube has 6 + 12 + 8 = 26 faces, edges and corners together, so 3 cubes have 3 × 26 = 78.» How many faces, edges and corners do 3 cubes have together? | 26 | 24 | *78 | 52
test: Sam says to cube a number means to multiply it by itself twice. Is Sam right? | Yes, because 2 × 2 is 4 | Yes, because twice means three times | *No, to cube a number multiplies it by itself three times, like 2 × 2 × 2 | No, because cube means a square shape
exam: «Heat, stirring and small grains all make dissolving faster, which is why loose sugar vanishes before a sugar cube does.» According to this sentence, what makes sugar dissolve faster? | Cold water and no stirring | Keeping it in a sealed box | *Heat and stirring | Big lumps of sugar
